1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,020
 One thing I'd like you to keep in mind is these people are not sadists, okay?

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,140
 I'm not saying there's no sadists among them.

3
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,280
 There's sadists in every single group.

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:14,240
 But they don't believe that they're hurting the chickens.

5
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,980
 They don't understand. They really don't.

6
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:23,920
 They're conditioned from birth to believe that this is okay and that the chickens don't feel pain.

7
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:31,660
 And if I'm in earshot of a little kid holding on to the mother's skirt and saying,

8
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:37,400
 the chickens are crying, and I hear the mother say, they're not crying.

9
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,160
 They're singing. They're happy to do this for you.

10
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:44,160
 I tell the mother, no, they're not. They're suffering.

11
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:46,600
 And I tell the little kid, you're right.

12
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:49,800
 This hurts the chickens.

13
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,500
 They're not singing. They're crying.

14
00:00:54,760 --> 00:01:02,200
 But it, you know, I mean, I think what we do is we try to plant seeds.

15
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:07,160
 And that's why we give the chickens a little relief before they're swung.

16
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:14,920
 And it's also good for the children to see that these are living creatures and that they need kindness.

17
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,560
 That they need, you know, the Talmud actually says,

18
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:23,960
 feed your chickens before you feed yourself.

19
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,340
 These chickens never get fed.

20
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:27,500
 They never get water.

21
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:36,740
 Many of them die in the crates from dehydration, starvation, exposure to the elements, infection, sepsis.

22
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,540
 I mean, it's really awful.

23
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:50,580
 And many times they're injured because the crates are thrown so violently and dragged, their feet break off, their toes and their feet break off.

24
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:54,960
 And we find, we find toes, you know, at these locations.

25
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,260
 It's really, really awful.

26
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:13,360
 And we, just so you know, we do not want anybody to rescue any chickens because we have a specific rescue team and we already have many, many.

27
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:28,000
 So, so, so we can only rescue as many as we have homes and, you know, we're, we're beyond capacity right now.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:49,620
 The only chickens who we're going to actually rescue tonight are ones who are relinquished to us and we have our dead, Dr. Cleary here, who's going to be evaluating them and helping us to identify the ones that are, that, that need serious rescue.

29
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:56,300
 And then we'll work with community affairs to try to negotiate them, um, to us.

30
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,240
 So, does anybody have any questions?

31
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,600
 Does anybody not want to be filmed at all?

32
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:03,160
 Yeah, me.

33
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,000
 I got you.

34
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,160
 Okay.

